   "text": "I read the drawing as a tetrahydropyran carrying four groups, and I assigned the stereochemistry from the wedges and hashes. Two chain lengths were hard to count in the image, so those are best guesses.\n\n**Tetrahydropyran ring** (O1, then C2 to C6):\n- C2 is the anomeric carbon. It carries a wedged OMe and the thiazolidinone C4 as a plain bond.\n- C3 is a CH2.\n- C4 carries the ester oxygen on a wedge.\n- C5 is a CH2.\n- C6 carries the alkenyl chain on a hash.\n\n**Chain on C6:** I counted a but-3-enyl group (CH2CH2CH=CH2). The drawing could also be read as pent-4-enyl, so this is uncertain.\n\n**Ester on C4:** I counted oct-7-enoate, C(=O) followed by five CH2 groups and CH=CH2. This could also be a shorter chain, so this count is uncertain too.\n\n**Thiazolidin-2-one:**\n- The ring is S1, C2(=O), N3, C4 and C5, with C5 a CH2.\n- N3 carries a PMB group, which is CH2-C6H4-OMe with the OMe para.\n- C4 carries a wedged H and is bonded to the pyran C2.\n\nI derived each @/@@ label by working out the neighbour order around the centre in the SMILES. For C6 and the thiazolidinone C4 the implicit H sits at the front or back, and for C2 the wedged OMe is the front substituent.\n\nSMILES: C=CCC[C@@H]1C[C@@H](OC(=O)CCCCCC=C)C[C@@](OC)(O1)[C@@H]2CSC(=O)N2Cc3ccc(OC)cc3"
